steps.message:
I wrote `/app/bin/summarize.py` and ran it on `/app/data`. The output is in `/app/out/summary.json`, and `tools/check_summary.py` reports that every value matches the reference figures. That check only covers the current files, so it says nothing about other exports.

The script follows the documented rules rather than anything specific to the current files. It handles:
- all eight depot formats;
- gzip, byte order marks, UTF-16 and `# charset:` encodings;
- directives and header rows that change part way through a file;
- ordering by `seq`;
- corrections, voids, resends and handovers;
- weights in kg, g, lb and oz, summed exactly and rounded only at the end;
- ship times converted to UTC.

One thing isn't spelled out in the docs. Some east rows carry their own weight unit as one extra field, placed right after the weight column. The script reads the unit from there. That is a guess from the current files, so a different placement in other exports would be missed.

I also wrote `/app/STATUS.json` with status `success`.
